  "header_assessment": "Six series form one coherent single-side-tagged acquisition set: axial PD FS, coronal PD FS, sagittal T2, sagittal PD FS, coronal T1 and an additional T1 sequence. All twelve sampled Laterality values are literal RIGHT; ImageLaterality and FrameLaterality are blank. SeriesNumbers3 through8, AcquisitionNumber1, one hashed PatientID, six hashed frames of reference. The two t1_se_cor_384 descriptions do not define two matching acquisitions: SeriesNumber6 has sagittal IOP agreeing with the other sagittal sequences, while SeriesNumber8 has coronal IOP. This is a description-orientation discrepancy, not proof of a second knee. No repeated full acquisition sets or mixed side tags are present.",
  "geometry_limits": "RIGHT is preserved literally rather than silently normalized to the DICOM R value, and is header evidence rather than anatomical confirmation. Six separate frame-of-reference hashes limit direct cross-series coordinate comparison. Only lexical endpoint samples have been inspected; they are not necessarily geometric extremes, and unsampled slices could differ. No full-file source digest or native anatomy verified in this follow-up.",
